AB  - To evaluate whether a CT radiomics-based machine learning classifier can predict histopathology of lymph nodes after post-chemotherapy retroperitoneal lymph node dissection in patients with metastatic non-seminomatous testicular germ cell tumors. Eighty patients, 204 segmented lymph nodes, 97 radiomic features each. A gradient-boosted tree achieved classification accuracy 0.81 in the validation dataset (sensitivity 88%, specificity 72%), versus 0.68 for a volume-only model. CT radiomics is a promising tool for predicting malignant histopathology in retroperitoneal lymph node metastases.
