AB  - Artificial intelligence techniques such as artificial neural networks, Bayesian belief networks and neuro-fuzzy modeling systems are complex mathematical models based on human neuronal structure. We reviewed basic concepts behind AI techniques and explored applications in various aspects of urological cancer management, including diagnosis, staging and prognostic prediction of prostate, bladder, kidney and testicular cancers. AI methods appear accurate and more explorative for analyzing large data cohorts and allow individualized prediction of disease behavior.
